\cf3 To optimize college costs, strategically reduce countable cash assets. Pay down high-interest consumer debt or make necessary large purchases like a car or home repairs. Maximize contributions to retirement accounts (401k, IRA), as these are not considered assets for FAFSA calculations. If you have a 529, parent-owned accounts are assessed at a lower rate than general savings. These actions can lower your Student Aid Index (SAI), potentially increasing financial aid eligibility. (Question: As a parent of a high school student, what should my short-term cash policy be to optimize my college costs?)\cell \row

