\cf3 A quotational loss, often called a "paper loss," is an unrealized loss on an investment you still hold. It occurs when the current market price (or "quotation") of your stock falls below the original purchase price. This loss reflects a temporary decrease in your portfolio's value, but it's not final. The loss only becomes "realized" if you sell the shares at that lower market price, thereby crystallizing the capital loss. (Question: What is quotational loss in stock market?)\cell \row

