\cf3 P/E multiples for private companies are not publicly available. Valuations typically use P/E ratios of comparable publicly traded companies, then apply discounts. Key adjustments include: * **Liquidity Discount:** Private shares are harder to sell. * **Size/Risk Discount:** Smaller, less diversified private companies often carry higher risk. * **Lack of Transparency:** Less stringent reporting than public firms. These factors generally result in lower P/E multiples for private companies compared to their public counterparts, even within the same industry. (Question: P/E multiples for privately held companies?)\cell \row

