\cf3 For retirement with annual compound interest and changing principal (due to contributions), combine two formulas. First, calculate the Future Value of an Annuity for your regular contributions: FV_annuity = C * [((1+r)^n - 1)/r] (C = annual contribution, r = annual interest rate, n = years) Then, add the Future Value of any initial principal: FV_initial = P * (1+r)^n (P = initial principal) The sum (FV_annuity + FV_initial) is your total projected retirement savings. (Question: Retirement formula for annual compound interest with changing principal)\cell \row

