\cf3 Generally, using long-term patterns for short-term investments is unreliable. Long-term trends smooth out daily volatility, which is critical for short-term trading decisions. Short-term price movements are primarily driven by immediate news, market sentiment, and specific technical indicators, not broad historical averages or multi-year cycles. Attempting to time quick trades based on long-term patterns can lead to significant misjudgments and increased risk due to the differing underlying drivers. (Question: Feasibility of using long term pattern on short term investments)\cell \row

